Surya N Kavuri (kavuri@lips.ecn.purdue.edu) wrote:
:     NH3.1 gives:
: 	(a) too many scrolls
: 	(b) too many potions
: 	(c) too many wands 

: 	By the time I finished with Gnomish Mines, I had about 15 blank
:     scrolls in most of the games I played.  Similarly, I could make 
:     15 odd water potions. All the stuff that the monsters carry in
:     NH3.1 has not be judged carefully in my opinion.  They seem to
:     have a lot of stuff in total and you could generate loads of goodies
:     from them.  Of course, a major limiting factor is that they limited
:     the scope of polypiling.

I don't think it unbalances the game.  Although I have built up caches of
holy water up to 25 and about 10 blank scrolls  and several wands there are 
balancing factors:

- A magic marker only writes on 1 scroll at a time
- Magic markers are rare, even in polypiles.  In several games with plenty
  of tools (from the town level) I have only gotten a magic marker in a
  polypile once.
- Potions of holy water are good for making good scrolls and potions
  great, but I don't seem able to use them as often as I would think.
  Once you max out your plusses on your weapons and armor, enchant armor
  and weapon scrolls aren't that good.  After that there isn't too much
  to bless.  Again I don't see too much game imbalance here.
- Good wands seem rare in polypiles.  I have never gotten another wand of
  polymorh or a book of polymorph.  I usually end up taking all the wands
  of create monster I can.
- I have used polypiling and useless potions and scrolls to make some
  pretty hefty characters, but the thing that makes me powerful is wishes
  and sacraficing, not tons of potions scrolls and wands.
- Have you ever tried to carry this stuff.  Without bags of holding, its
  pretty hard.  I usually try to get one as soon as I get my gauntlets of
  power, usually polypiling the tools from the gnome mines.

I agree that nethack 3.1 is easier than 3.0, but it has so much more
variety than 3.0 that it is funner.
